                            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %p
            This is a subentry of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            about the
            = succeed "." do
              %em plus-construction on presheaves
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plus+construction"} plus construction
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#construction_of_sheafification"} Construction of sheafification
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em plus construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^+ : PSh(C) \to PSh(C)
            on presheaves over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an operation that makes a presheaf “closer” to being a sheaf.
          %p
            For ordinary sheaves of sets, the plus construction replaces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            first by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+presheaf"} separated presheaf
            and then by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                  %mi SepPSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PSh(C) \stackrel{(-)^+}{\to} SepPSh(C)
                  \\stackrel{(-)^+}{\to} Sh(C)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (The first of these steps, however, is not a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflection
            into
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SepPsh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SepPsh(C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated"} n-truncated
            morphisms, a presheaf is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                separated precisely if every comparison map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Desc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(U) \to Desc(A,U)
                to the set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+data"} descent data
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %li
              %p
                a sheaf precisely if every such comparison map is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-2%29-truncated"} (-2)-truncated
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
          %p
            More generally, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-topos"} (n,1)-topos
            theory, the plus-construction is applied
            = succeed "-times" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            %span.newWikiWord
              (n,1)-presheaf
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%28n%2C1%29-presheaf"} ?
            (a presheaf of
            = succeed "-groupoids)," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-sheaf"} (n,1)-sheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ALS"} Anel and Leena Subramaniam, 2020
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie, section 6.5.3
          %h2#definition Definition
          #PlusConstruction.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a small site equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:C^{op}\to Set
              be a functor. Then the
              %strong plus construction
              is a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^+ : PSh(C) \to PSh(C)
              defined by the following equivalent descriptions:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi colim
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi R
                            %mo ↪
                            %mi y
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi J
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mi Psh
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+(U) = colim_{(R\hookrightarrow  y U)\in J(U)} Hom_{Psh(C)}(R,A)
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(U)
                  can be defined in any of the following equivalent ways:
                %ul
                  %li
                    The poset of covering
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieves"} sieves
                    on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                    for the topology. (It is important here that we use covering
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em sieves
                  %li
                    The class of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+monomorphisms"} dense monomorphisms
                    with
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
                    codomain
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi y
                            %mi U
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y U
                  %li
                    The class of monomorphisms with codomain
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y U
                    that are inverted by the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
                    functor. (Of course, this definition is not available unless we have shown that sheafification exists in some other way.)
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\in C^{op}
                  we define
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+(U)
                  to be the set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
                  of pairs
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,s)
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\in J(U)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi dom
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s=(s_f\in A(dom f)|f\in R)
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matching+family"} compatible family
                  of elements of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  relative to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi s
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,s)\sim (R', s')
                  iff there is a
                  = succeed "-covering" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo ″
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi R
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R'' \subseteq R \cap R'
                  on which the restrictions of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s'
                  agree.
              %li
                %p
                  In the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
                  of the presheaf topos
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo +
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi K
                          %mo ⊆
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi K
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mtext is a singleton
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ∼
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+ = \{ K \subseteq A \,|\, j(K\,\text{ is a singleton}) \}/{\sim}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∼
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
                  is the equivalence relation given by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ∼
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \sim L
                  if and only if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo =
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(K = L)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                  is the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Lan
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi r
                              %mi op
                        %msub
                          %mi Ran
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi s
                              %mi op
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+ = Lan_{r^{op}} Ran_{s^{op}} A
                  , where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo :
                        %mi J
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r : J \to C
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
                  of the functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cov
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi Pos
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cov : C^{op} \to Pos
                  sending each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  to its set of covering
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieves"} sieves
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:C\to J
                  sends each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\in C
                  to its maximal sieve
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_U
                  (the set of all morphisms with codomain
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            The first and last of these definitions also work for higher sheaves on higher sites, i.e. when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-site"} (infinity,1)-site
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Gpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:C^{op} \to \infty Gpd
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-presheaf"} (infinity,1)-presheaf
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h2#construction_of_sheafification Construction of sheafification
          %p
            The basic property of the plus-construction is that we can construct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
            (a.k.a. stack completion, in the higher-categorical case) by iterating it. For ordinary presheaves of sets, two iterations suffice: for any presheaf
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+
            is separated, while if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is separated then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+
            is a sheaf; thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{++}
            is the sheafification of any presheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Note, though, that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi SepPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^+ : PSh(C) \to SepPSh(C)
              is not left adjoint to the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mo :
                    %mi SepPSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota : SepPSh(C) \hookrightarrow PSh(C)
              of the full subcategory of separated presheaves. If it were, it would be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflector"} reflector
              and therefore satisfy
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi ι
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi Id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^+ \circ \iota \cong Id
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/49486/the-single-plus-construction-is-not-the-left-adjoint-of-the-inclusion-of-separat"} this MathOverflow question
              for details.
          %p
            More generally, when working with presheaves of
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
            iterations for the plus-construction to converge to a sheaf/stack. In the case
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=\infty
          %p
            We now sketch a proof of these facts, using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/implicit+infinity-category+convention"} implicit infinity-category convention
            so that our results apply to higher sheaves/stacks as well as ordinary ones.
          %p
            We use the fourth definition above
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi r
                          %mi op
                    %msub
                      %mi Ran
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi s
                          %mi op
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+ = Lan_{r^{op}} Ran_{s^{op}} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+ = r_! s_* A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to A^+
          %p
          #AnAdjointQuadruple.num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:C\to J
              is right adjoint to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo :
                      %mi J
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:J\to C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇄
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* : Psh(C) \rightleftarrows Psh(J) : s^*
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_! \dashv r^* \dashv s^* \dashv s_*.
            %p
              Moreover,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^*
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_*
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_!
              preserves finite limits, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(J)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive
              and even
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+connected+topos"} totally connected
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(C)
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Since the maximal sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_U
              is the terminal object of the fiber of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              picks out a fiberwise terminal object in the fibration
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple#KanExtensionOfAdjointPairIsAdjointQuadruple"} here
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r s = 1_C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              is fully faithful, and hence so are
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_*
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mo !
                      %mo ≅
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_! \cong r^*
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^{op}
              are filtered since covering sieves are closed under intersections, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_!
              preserves finite limits since finite limits commute with filtered colimits.
          %p
            Thus, we can identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Psh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(C)
            with either the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects"} discrete objects
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+objects"} codiscrete objects
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(J)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^*
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Psh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Psh(C)
            as the discrete object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^*A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* r_! s_* s^* r^* A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^*(A^+)
            can be written as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mo ♯
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; \sharp r^* A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ʃ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; = r^* r_!
            is the reflector into the discrete objects and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♯
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp = s_* s^*
            is the reflector into the codiscrete objects.
          %p
            The rest of the proof can actually be carried out “synthetically” in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            of the cohesive topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(J)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HoTTplus"} in the HoTT/Coq library
          %p
          #PlusWellPointed.num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              The plus-construction is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+endofunctor"} well-pointed endofunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : A \to A^+
              and a homotopy (an equality in the case
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo +
                      %mo ∼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta : \eta_{A^+} \sim (\eta_A)^+
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \eta_A
              is homotopic to the naturality square
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo +
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∼
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{A^+} \circ \eta_A \sim (\eta_A)^+ \circ \eta_A
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              This follows fairly formally from its identification with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mo ♯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; \sharp
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p The plus-construction preserves finite limits.
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Both functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_!
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_*
              preserve finite limits.
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Psh(C)
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a sheaf.
              %li
                The canonical map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* A \to s_* A
                is an equivalence.
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* A
                is codiscrete.
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A \to A^+
                is an equivalence.
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A \to A^+
                has a retraction.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              To see that the first two are equivalent, note that for a covering sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r^* A)(R) = A(U)
              while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s_* A)(R)
              is the space of descent data for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mo ♯
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_* A \cong s_* s^* r^* A = \sharp r^* A
            %p
              For the fourth, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^*A
              is codiscrete, then it is equivalent to
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♯
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp r^* A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ʃ
                      %mo ♯
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643; \sharp r^* A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A
              is an equivalence, it has a retraction. Finally, if it has a retraction, then the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mo ♯
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp r^* A \to &amp;#643; \sharp r^* A = r^* A^+
              is a retraction for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mo ♯
                      %msup
                        %mi r
                        %mo *
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^* A \to \sharp r^* A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^*A
              is codiscrete.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If some (perhaps transfinite) iteration of the plus-construction on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Psh(C)
              stabilizes, it is a sheaf and the sheafification of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p This follows formally from the fact that the plus-construction is a well-pointed endofunctor whose fixed points are the sheaves.
          %p
            Now since the plus-construction is an accessible endofunctor of a locally presentable category, its iteration always converges at some transfinite stage. It follows that sheafification exists. (Roughly this argument appears in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie, section 6.5.3
          %p
            We now want to prove that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a presheaf of
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
            steps. Though long expected, it seems that this was first actually proven by
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#ALS"} Anel and Leena Subramaniam, 2020
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Psh(C)
              is
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-separated
              if the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A\to A^+
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated"} n-truncated
          %p
            Thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a sheaf if and only if it is
            = succeed "-separated." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            = succeed "-truncated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-groupoids)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+
            and hence so is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A
            = succeed "-truncated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-separated." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            We will prove that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            = succeed "-separated," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
            steps. The central auxiliary definition is:
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(C)
              is
              %strong plus-connected
              if there is a lift in its
              = succeed "-naturality" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:B \to A^+
              and homotopies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo +
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^+ h \sim \eta_B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h f \sim \eta_A
              that paste to the naturality square
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                      %mo ∼
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi B
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^+ \eta_A \sim \eta_B f
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              For any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Psh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A\to A^+
              is plus-connected.
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PlusWellPointed"}
              says precisely that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{A^+}
              is a lift in the
              = succeed "-naturality" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
              is plus-connected, so is its diagonal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ▵
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \triangle f : A \to A\times_B A
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p Since the plus-construction preserves finite limits, it suffices to observe that if a given commutative square has a lift, so does the induced square between its diagonals.
          %p So far everything has been very formal. The concrete input from the fact that we are talking about a Grothendieck topology comes here:
          %p
          #Composing.num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} monomorphism
              that is plus-connected, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo +
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^+ : A^+ \to B^+
              is an equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Since the plus-construction preserves finite limits, it preserves monomorphisms; thus it suffices to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^+
              is surjective. An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in B^+(U)
              is determined by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matching+family"} matching family
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+sieve"} covering sieve
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi y
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\hookrightarrow y U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_V \in B(V)
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\to U
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is plus-connected, we have a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:B\to A^+
              assigning to each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_V
              an object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(x_V) \in A^+(V)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi V
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi y
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_V \hookrightarrow y V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              to obtain a covering sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              (which is equal to
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^+
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge -1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
              is
              = succeed "-truncated" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo +
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^+ : A^+ \to B^+
              is
              = succeed "-truncated." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By induction. The base case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=-1
              is the previous lemma. For the inductive step,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is
              = succeed "-truncated" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ▵
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \triangle f
              is
              = succeed "-truncated" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ▵
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\triangle f)^+
              is
              = succeed "-truncated." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ▵
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\triangle f)^+
              is equivalent to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ▵
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \triangle (f^+)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^+
              is
              = succeed "-truncated." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is
              = succeed "-separated," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
              steps.
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is
              = succeed "-separated," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A\to A^+
              is
              = succeed "-truncated," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\eta_A)^+
              is
              = succeed "-truncated." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{A^+}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^+
              is
              = succeed "-separated." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %p
              Thus, by induction, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is
              = succeed "-separated," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+2)
              = succeed "-separated," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-(n+2))
              = succeed "-separated," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-2)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Note that we do not need to know that the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              is obtained as the category of covering sieves for a topology on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:J\to C
              that is a fibration with cofiltered fibers and a fully faithful right adjoint, plus the result of Lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Composing"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              could be a “mono-saturated lex modulator” in the sense of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#ALS"} ALS
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(C)
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              We can also construct left exact localizations of non-presheaf toposes in this way. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a topos that is itself a left exact localization of some presheaf topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              induces a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              as above, and by composing the reflectors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ʃ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#643;
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              with the reflection into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              we can make the same argument work to construct a left exact localization of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheafification"} (∞,1)-sheafification
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Related entries:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
          %p
            A standard textbook reference in the context of 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            is:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+elephant"} Sketches of an elephant
                  \- a topos theory compendium
          %p
            Remarks on the plus-construction in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (infinity,1)-topos theory
            is in section 6.5.3 of
          %ul#Lurie
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p The plus-construction for presheaves in values in abelian categories is also called the Heller-Rowe construction:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Heller"}> Alex Heller
              , K. A. Rowe,
              %em On the category of sheaves
              %p
                Amer. J. Math. 84 1962 205–216,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=144341"} MR144341
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2307/2372759"} doi
          %p
            The plus-construction is studied for higher sheaves, and shown to converge after
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n+2
            steps for
            = succeed "-presheaves," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li#ALS
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathieu+Anel"}> Mathieu Anel
              , Chaitanya Leena Subramaniam.
              = succeed "." do
                %em Small object arguments, plus-construction, and left-exact localizations
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.00731"} arxiv:2004.00731
          %p
            The above argument is formalized in the internal logic of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Psh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(J)
            here:
          %ul
            %li#HoTTplus
              Canonical binary meets of subuniverses,
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/blob/master/theories/Modalities/Meet.v"} https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/blob/master/theories/Modalities/Meet.v
